Where P_0 is the vapor pressure at 100°C, ΔHvap is the enthalpy of vaporization of water (40.8 kJ/mol), R is the gas constant (8.314 J/mol·K), T is the temperature in Kelvin, and T_b is the boiling point in Kelvin.

