","Amino acids are classified based on their metabolic flux, meaning the sequence of metabolic steps they undergo in the body. This classification is based on the metabolic intermediates they are converted into during the breakdown of amino acids. The metabolic flux of an amino acid is crucial for understanding its synthesis, regulation, and the potential metabolic constraints of the body.

