The cost of the remaining 140 kilometers is:
\[
140 \times \frac{2}{3} = \frac{280}{3} \text{ km}
\]

The total charge for 150 kilometers is:
\[
90 + \frac{280}{3} = \frac{270 + 280}{3} = \frac{550}{3} \approx 183.33 \text{ km}
\]

