- \( N = 100 \) turns
- \( I = 1 \, \text{A} \)
- \( r = 0.2 \, \text{m} \)
- \( \mu_0 = 4\pi \times 10^{-7} \, \text{T m/A} \)

\[
B = \frac{(4\pi \times 10^{-7} \, \text{T m/A})}{2\pi} \frac{100 \times 1}{0.2}
\]
\[
B = 2 \times 10^{-7} \, \text{T m/A} \times 500
\]
\[
B = 1000 \times 10^{-7} \, \text{T}
\]
\[
B = 10^{-4} \, \text{T}
\]

Thus, the magnetic field strength at the center of the coil is \(\boxed{10^{-4} \, \text{T}}\).
