","The net chemical reaction that occurs during the discharging of a lead storage battery is:
\[
\text{Pb} + \text{PbO}_2 + 2\text{H}^+ + 2\text{H}_2\text{O} \rightarrow 2\text{Pb(OH)}_2 + \text{H}_2
\]
This reaction is a single displacement reaction where the lead (Pb) combines with the lead oxide (PbO₂) and water (H₂O) to form zinc hydroxide (Zn(OH)₂). The overall reaction is:
\[
\text{Pb} + \2\text{PbO}_2 + 4\text{H}_2\text{O} \rightarrow 4\text{ZnSO}_4 + \text{O}_2
\]

