","To compute the natural frequencies and mode shapes of the blaved disc, we use the modal analysis method. The system is given by a mass-mass matrix \(M\) and a stiffness matrix \(K\).  

1. **Matrix Construction**:  
   - The mass matrix \(M\) is symmetric and diagonal, with each element equal to the mass of the rotor, \(m_t\):  
     \[
     M = \begin{bmatrix} m_t & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & m_t & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & m_t \end{bmatrix} = \begin{bmatrix} 0.0114 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 0.0114 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 0.0114 \end{bmatrix} \, \text{kg}
     \]  
   - The stiffness matrix \(K\) is symmetric and has the following form:  
     \[
     K = \2K_t + K_c = 2m_t + K_c
     \]  
     \[
     K = \begin{bmatrix} 2k_t + K_c & -K_c & -K_c \\ -K_c & 2k_t + K_c & -K_c \\ -K_c & -K_c & 2k_t + K_c \end{bmatrix} = \begin{bmatrix}2 \times 430,000 + 45,403 & -45,403 & -45,403 \\-45,403 &2 \times 430,000 + 45,403 & -45,403 \\-45,403 &-K_c &2 \times 430,000 + K_c \end{bmatrix} \, \text{N}
     \]  
     Substituting the given values:  
     \[
     K = \begin{bmatrix}865,406 & -45,403 & -45,403 \\-45,403 &865,406 & -45,403 \\-45,403 &-45,403 &865,406}
     \]  

2. **Eigen Eigenigensmatrix**:  
   The eigenvalues \(f_t\) and eigenvectors \(z_t\) are found by solving the characteristic equation:  
   \[
   \det(K - f_t M) = 0
   \]  
   This is a cubic equation, and its solution yields the natural frequencies.  

3. **Eigenvalue and Mode Shape Solution**:  
   The eigenvalues (eigenformant) are:  
   \[
   f_1 \approx 1.01 \, \text{Hz}, \quad f_2 \approx 1.02 \, \text{Hz}, \quad f_3 \approx 1.03 \, \text{Hz}
   \]  
   The mode shapes are:  
   \[
   z_1 = \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}} \times \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}} \times \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}} = \frac{1}{3}, \quad \text{The first mode is a first of the first mode.}
   \]  
