\[
\Delta \eta = F_{\text{fr}} \Delta x
\]
where \( \Delta x \) is the distance traveled by the object (or in this case, the horizontal displacement of the object due to friction). The work dissipated is equal to the work done by the friction force:
\[
\Delta \eta = -\int_0^{\Delta x} f_{\text{fr}} \, dx = -\int_0^{\Delta x} f_{\text{fr}} \, dx
\]
The friction force \( F_{\text{fr}} \) is proportional to the coefficient of friction \( \mu \) and the normal force \( F_N \), and the normal force is equal to the weight of the object:
\[
F_{\text{fr}} = \mu F_N = \mu mg
\]
Thus, the work dissipated is:
\[
\Delta \eta = -\mu mg \Delta x
\]
Thus, the entropy production rate is:
\[
\pi_S = \frac{\Delta \eta}{T} = \frac{\eta}{T} = \frac{\mu \eta g \Delta x}{T}
\]
